WHY THIS FILE STAYS, BEYOND THE LICENCE
---------------------------------------

The product surface carries no third-party identity — that is enforced in CI by
`tooling/ci/brand-scan.mjs`, and it is the correct and normal treatment for a
licensed codebase. Externally this is our platform.

Internally, the engineers who maintain this code need to know what it is:

  * It targets JRE 8 and Spring Boot 1.5.9, with MySQL, MongoDB, Redis, Kafka
    and Zookeeper versions from the 2011-2019 range. Tracking upstream security
    advisories requires knowing which upstream to track.

  * `01_wallet_rpc/` handles private key material for BTC, ETH, USDT, LTC, EOS
    and others. `custody-scan` (Doctrine §16.10) does not cover Java and does
    not read this tree.

  * 31 `.jar` files are committed as binary dependencies rather than declared
    Maven coordinates. They cannot be verified against a published checksum and
    they sit on the classpath of services that hold custody.

  * The upstream README states the operating exchange ceased trading and that
    the author disclaims responsibility for commercial use.

A team that believes this code is original will not know to check any of the
above. Removing this file would not make the code safer; it would only make it
harder to defend.

See docs/adr/2026-07-28-coinexchange-integration.md for the integration
decisions, including the unresolved question of which system owns a balance.
